  "label": "Pop Art Movement",
  "description": "Pop Art is an art movement that emerged in the mid-20th century, particularly in the 1950s and 1960s, characterized by the use of imagery from popular culture, advertising, and mass media. It often features bold colors, repetition, and irony. The painting in the background of the image, depicting stylized dog heads in vibrant colors, is a clear reference to Pop Art, specifically reminiscent of Andy Warhol's style. This artistic context adds to the ironic or satirical tone of the meme, as the juxtaposition of a serious subject (lie detector test) with a playful, commercial art style enhances the humor.",
